# Optional integrations. Nothing in this bundle requires any of them, and the
# whole package works with this file absent.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill only what you use. `.env` is gitignored; never commit
# a filled copy.

# --- Storage -----------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL connection string, used only when storage.backend is `postgres` in
# config/default.yaml. Read from the environment on purpose: a DSN in a YAML
# file is a DSN in git.
# LNI_POSTGRES_DSN=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/lni

# --- Configuration -----------------------------------------------------------
# A directory of *.yaml files layered on top of config/. This is where to keep a
# filled profile, ICPs and service categories, outside the repository.
# LNI_CONFIG_DIR=/home/you/.config/lni

# --- What is deliberately absent ---------------------------------------------
# There is no LinkedIn credential here, and there is no variable to add one.
# This bundle does not sign in to LinkedIn, does not hold a session cookie, and
# does not call any LinkedIn endpoint. If you hold authorised access to an
# official LinkedIn API, the integration point is documented in
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and is left unimplemented rather than faked.
